  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Nigerians usually carry an English or Christian first name (Daniel, Blessing) or a Muslim one (Ibrahim, Aisha), and a first name in their own language, often both, and the family name is usually the father's. Yoruba names say something: Oluwaseun (God has done it), Ayodele (joy has come home); they shorten to Seun, Ayo, Tunde, Bisi, Kemi. Igbo names often praise God (Chukwuemeka, Chiamaka, Chinedu, Ngozi, from Chi or Chukwu, God). Hausa names are mostly Muslim names in Hausa form (Musa, Aisha, Abubakar, Hauwa) with nicknames like Mallam for a respected man. Ibibio names include Emem (peace), Ubong (glory), Mfon (goodness), Itoro (praise). Ijaw names from the Niger Delta include Tamuno, Ebi, Ibinabo, Boma, Preye.",
